  "description": "R-PAR-1 PAR-ERROR, SQL-DEMAND, SQL-REL: At which call does each error kind appear, and with which number and description, when row id 3 is the first bad row: 1 / (id - 3); CByte(id * 100); CLng of a non-numeric Text; Sqr(id - 4); Log(id - 3); CDate of a non-date Text; 2147483645 + id; and for constant expressions with no column (1 / 0, CByte(300), CLng('x'), alone and beside id), does the error appear at OpenRecordset or at a row (one GetRows(5) per statement)? Runs on a fresh copy of r-par-1-error opened read-only through DAO OpenDatabase in one process and one STA; each statement is opened with Database.OpenRecordset as a snapshot unless stated, and every call's result, HRESULT and DBEngine.Errors are captured.",
